# Cursor Cloud specific instructions

These notes apply only to Cursor Cloud agents (kept out of the shared `AGENTS.md` since T3 Code is
developed in many places). They cover the VM environment and non-obvious run caveats.

## Toolchain

`install` puts Vite+ on the login-shell PATH. Login shells (`bash -lc`) resolve:

- Node 24.22.0 (satisfies `engines.node` `^24.13.1`) from
  `~/.local/share/vite-plus/fallback-bin` (runtime under `~/.local/share/vite-plus/js_runtime`)
- pnpm 11.10.0, matching `packageManager`
- `vp` 1.2.0 from `~/.local/share/vite-plus/bin`

`~/.profile` ends with the `t3code-cloud-toolchain` PATH line so those directories win over
`/exec-daemon/node` (Node 22) and nvm's Node 22. Non-login shells still see Node 22. Run commands
in a login shell (`bash -lc '...'`).

`vp` is the package manager and task runner (`vp i`, `vp test run <files>`,
`vp run --filter <pkg> <script>`). `vp i` prints ENOENT warnings while linking `vite` and `vitest`
bins. The catalog aliases `vite` to `@voidzero-dev/vite-plus-core`, and the real packages are
installed. `vp test` and `vp run dev` use that toolchain.

`vp check` also runs the formatter (not just lint); markdown edits must be formatter-clean. Run
`vp check --fix` before committing.

## Running the web app

On boot, `start` launches `vp run dev` in a tmux session named `t3-dev` and waits until the pane
prints `pairingUrl:`. Read ports from the `[dev-runner]` line. With the default offset that is web
`5733` and server `13773`. The web process listens on IPv6 localhost (`::1`); `127.0.0.1:5733`
refuses connections. The server listens on `127.0.0.1`.

Leave `VITE_HTTP_URL` and `VITE_WS_URL` unset. Leave `T3CODE_HOME` unset. Dev state is created under
`~/.t3/dev` (for example `~/.t3/dev/statev2.sqlite`), not `~/.t3/userdata`.

Open the pairing URL from the `t3-dev` pane before the web UI can talk to the server. Do not commit
or publish that URL. The dev runner may attach the current workspace as a project on startup.

Agent providers are external CLIs (`codex`, `claude`, `cursor-agent`, `opencode`) probed on `PATH`.
Without one installed the UI loads and accepts a turn, then reports that the provider CLI is
missing. Provider probing runs at startup and refreshes roughly every 5 minutes — restart the dev
server to pick up a newly installed provider CLI.

## Android native builds (apps/mobile)

The Android SDK is not installed. This VM has no `/dev/kvm`, so an emulator will not run. The
mobile README documents iOS for local builds and routes Android through EAS.

A full `:app:assembleDebug` is also blocked in the app itself: `patches/react-native-screens@4.25.2.patch`
adds codegen props (`subtitle`, `largeSubtitle`, `navigationItemStyle`,
`headerCenterBarButtonItems`, `headerToolbarItems`) without Android Kotlin setters, so the generated
`ScreenStackHeaderConfigManagerInterface` is unimplemented.

## Known flaky tests (unrelated to setup)

- `apps/server/src/git/GitManager.test.ts` (cross-repo PR metadata, can time out at 12s).
- `apps/server/src/provider/ProviderRegistry.test.ts` (codex binaryPath re-probe ordering).
